@page "/access-denied"
@* Reached only by the cookie authentication handler's AccessDeniedPath (configured in
   ManagementUiAuthentication) after a static server-side render's [Authorize] check fails --
   Blazor's own <NotAuthorized> fragment in Routes.razor only applies to interactive rendering,
   which this app doesn't use, so a denied static SSR request never reaches it. Deliberately not
   [Authorize]-attributed: the whole point is to be reachable by a signed-in user who just failed
   an authorization check. *@

<h1>Not authorised</h1>
<p>
    Your account does not hold the role this page requires. Roles are assigned in Microsoft Entra
    ID; ask a platform administrator if you believe this is wrong.
</p>
